-DE-NeRF is a method for modeling rapidly moving and deforming scenes by combining RGB and event camera data [S1, unofficial]. It jointly optimizes camera poses and radiance fields, leveraging the high-speed, asynchronous nature of event cameras to capture visual changes alongside sparse RGB frames [S1, unofficial]. Unlike static decomposition methods, DE-NeRF explicitly handles temporal dynamics through event-based pose estimation, while decomposing the scene into geometric, diffuse, and specular components to enable relighting and appearance editing [S2].
